Context: the Concrete project, branch wip/legacy-sweep-2 (the whole branch against its base). legacy/ is a frozen copy of the old implementation; scripts/checks/legacy_frozen.sh enforces that it changes only by byte-for-byte sweeps recorded in scripts/checks/legacy.lock, whose ONE parser and reader is scripts/checks/lib/legacy_lock.py (line 1 `base <oid>`, line 2 `tree <oid>`, then `sweep <oid> <oid>` rows, LF-terminated; it refuses NUL, CR, non-ASCII, malformed and repeated rows, a missing line 2 and an unterminated last line). History is judged against trusted history (main's first-parent chain; LEGACY_TRUSTED_REF). Failures of the parser or of helper commands must fail closed (`refused: <step> failed (exit N)`), never read as "no problems". doc_links.py takes lock rows from the parser. scripts/checks/sandbox_isolation.sh passes the trusted base to its probe. Check the parser, every consumer, fail-closed behaviour, the controls (exact diagnostics, load-bearing), the swept files, and the docs/changelog.
